{"t": 1794106242.0395696, "kind": "call", "tool": "gitlab_create_merge_request_thread", "args": {"body": "**Root cause of the red `main` pipeline** (pipeline #8812, job `test:contract` #77104):\n\n`billing/invoice.py::invoice_number()` formatted the sequence without zero-padding, so it returned `INV-2026-42`. The contract test `contract/test_invoice.py::test_invoice_number_format` encodes the Finance ERP import format from FIN-77, which requires the sequence part to be zero-padded to 6 digits:\n\n```\nAssertionError: assert 'INV-2026-42' == 'INV-2026-000042'\n```\n\n**Fix** \u2014 pad the sequence to 6 digits with `:06d`:\n\n```python\ndef invoice_number(year: int, seq: int) -> str:\n    return f\"INV-{year}-{seq:06d}\"\n```\n\nWith this change `invoice_number(2026, 42)` returns `INV-2026-000042`, so the failing contract assertion passes. The `lint` job is unaffected. This is the padded invoice-number format the ERP v2 switch in this MR needs, so the same change should be part of this branch before it is merged back to `main`.", "merge_request_iid": "12", "project_id": "acme/billing-legacy"}, "ok": true}
